Explanation:
 We mostly ban packages in prisonpc-bad-package-conflicts-everyone.
 This works well, and we get clear error messages.
 But it cannot block by source package, and cannot glob of package names.
 In here, block things that prisonpc-bad-package-conflicts-everyone cannot.
 .
 If you try to install a package blocked here,
 the error message will be something like this:
     E: Package 'libc6-dev' has no installation candidate
 .
 One benefit of blocking things explicitly here is that measure-install-footprints.py
 will skip them before measuring them, i.e. runs faster.
 .
 Use an arbitrary negative number instead of -1, so
 it is easier to git grep for that number across the codebase,
 when you see it in apt policy output.
 .
 FIXME: some of this could be folded back into prisonpc-bad-package-conflicts.
 NOTE: nfs-client needs src:lvm2.
 NOTE: dbus-x11 (banned) is for syvinit; dbus-user-session is for systemd.
 NOTE: mbim and qmi are for 3G/LTE modems, and not linked by anything we want.
 NOTE: apt needs sqv|gpg, so block sq and other sq components EXCEPT sqv, for now.
 NOTE: xdm/xfce4-session need cpp
 NOTE: blocking src:gnome-online-accounts blocks apps like gnome-music and geary
 NOTE: udisks2 (mount/eject DVDs) needs libfdisk* and fdisk and libparted*
 NOTE: gbrainy needs mono-gac and mono-runtime (src:mono)
 NOTE: systemd needs libcryptsetup (src:cryptsetup)
 NOTE: bash and util-linux need src:ncurses (can block ncurses6 but not ncursesw6)
 NOTE: prisonpc-openttd-extras needs timidity needs libncurses6 :-(
 NOTE: openssh-client (staff-only) needs src:libfido2
 NOTE: libgl1-mesa needs libllvmNN (src:llvm-toolchain-NN)
